it's another new year how many of you  have written down your new year's  resolution here's a fun fact every  single year losing weight is the number  one resolution across the world  everybody wants to be slimmer healthier  it better or to feel better but before  we continue grab your phone and download  the life Sam app watch this video  through and follow along all right see  if this sounds familiar for the first  month  everything seems on track you're doing  really well and you're hitting all your  fitness goals come February you fall off  the wagon and you're forgotten all the  new year's resolution you wrote a month  ago and you sort of like just push it  aside and tell yourself I'll try it  again next year and the same cycle  repeats again for another year and  another year and this goes on for  several years and you're stuck in the  same situation I don't want this for you  I want you to succeed so I'm going to  teach you seven really simple but  effective steps to start a successful  fitness resolution let's do this  together all right the first step is to  actually write it down most of the time  we tell our self what we want to achieve  without physically writing it down it  has been proven that people who write  down their goals are more likely to  achieve them by over 70% so I want you  to start getting into the habit of  taking notes you can either write it in  your journal or if you're more of a  mobile person then take note in your  mobile and make that your wallpaper  don't just write your fitness resolution  and leave the rest of the pages blank  start to develop the habit of journaling  every single day it can be a list of  things to accomplish for the day three  things you're grateful for and three  things that you can improve on the habit  of keeping a journal will drive you to  reflect it will remind you of your goals  hence you are more likely to stay  committed and achieve success the next  question is what should I write that  leads on to my next step be detailed but  at the same time don't stress out about  it there is no right or wrong and  sometimes you would even know what you  want until you start writing things down  so the life some app is a great app to  help you achieve your fitness and  lifestyle goals by offering you a  personalized guide to healthy living so  when you sign up  it'll ask you what your fitness goal is  is it to be healthier to lose weight or  to gain weight instead of just saying my  goal is to lose weight let's dive deeper  my goal is to lose 20 kilos this year  now go ahead and key in your current  weight and key in your goal weight  that's a great start now let's dive in  even deeper and break it down so my goal  is to lose 20 kilos this year and I'm  going to achieve that by losing an  average of 0.5 kilos or week go ahead  and set your goal when you add quantity  to your goals and break them down to  smaller goals you're able to measure and  track and to ensure success so rather  than looking at a bigger goal of losing  20 kilos which can be overwhelming and  scary you're focusing on the small  achievable goal of 0.5 kilos per week so  guys setting a goal is only one small  part of the puzzle the next step is the  most important step have an action plan  how are you going to achieve your goal  what do you have to do more off what do  you have to sacrifice so right now I  want you to create two columns the first  column is the action column what do you  have to do more off the second column is  the give column what do you have to give  up so the action column can be I'll hit  the gym at least three times weekly I'll  aim to cook two healthy meals a day the  gift column can be out order take away  only once a week I'll have to wake up an  hour earlier to hit the gym I'll only go  out for a drink once a week it doesn't  have to be a long list but rather a  short list which you can focus on and  turn them into positive habits so with  the lifestyle app when you sign up for  lose weight you also have access to a  three-week meal plan with four meals per  day the recipes are really easy to cook  and contain  maximum of five ingredients you also  have a meal planner where you can see  and plan what to eat for the coming days  you also get a shopping list to bring  with you to the grocery store way  cheaper than any other meal plants out  there on top of that you'll start to  learn what healthy ingredients are and  the right portion servings and you will  also get to cheat on some days and still  meet your goal hey I believe it's all  about balance and moderation one of the  key factors when it comes to lifestyle  change is planning and keeping it simple  with a really clear and easy meal plan  and also shopping lists it will reduce  your chances of buying junk when you're  out doing your grocery shopping the next  step is to turn your resolution into a  habit now that you have a clear goal and  an action plan the next step is to put  them into practice daily and to turn  them into positive habits the best way  to break bad habits it's not to try to  stop doing them  because by doing that you're  subconsciously giving your bad habits  even more attention we plan to set  negative goals and focus on the things  we're not going to do for instance I'm  not going to eat a junk food  I'm not going to binge eat instead of  focusing on what you're not going to do  and fight against it the goal is to  create new positive habit and focus on  what you're going to do so for instance  I'm going to have at least five servings  of vegetables every day I'm going to  drink at least eight glasses of water  and I'm going to hit the gym at least  three times weekly rewire your mind  focus on your new positive habits and  work on them daily it's about making  slow and subtle changes to give your  body and mind the time to adapt and  adjust so I've created a video on 10  steps to break that habit and to achieve  your goal do check it out another great  feature I love about the lifestyle app  is the ability to track your fitness  progress every time you consume one  serving of vegetables hit the veggie  icon  every time you drink one cup of water  hit the drink icon take pictures and  track all your food intake and also your  daily activities it's a really fun and  effective way to remind you to stick to  your action plan and at the end of the  day when you review your progress you  can either look for ways to improve or  celebrate small successes along the way  if you commit to check your progress  every single day eventually eating well  and staying active will become part of  you step number six share and be part of  a community every year I'll drag my list  and exchange it with a close friend I  truly believe that when you share your  goals with like-minded people it will  give you a sense of accountability and  they're able to offer you help and  support when things get tough but not  this who you share your goals with is  extremely important I wouldn't encourage  you to just open up and share it with  everyone and anybody you know over  sharing might not be a positive thing  because these people may end up  sabotaging you oh she's trying to lose  weight how much have you lost  come on one slice of cake will not hurt  you the harsh truth is not everybody  will be excited about your goals there  will always be that one or two people  who have tried to bring you down and you  don't need that energy in your life only  share with those who truly care and want  the best for you together you can keep  each other updated get tips advice and  support each other and the final tip is  to remember this is not just another new  year resolution it is a permanent  lifestyle change it's not something you  do and then stop once you've lost X  amount of weight but rather it is about  setting a pathway to a healthier and  happier life forever so you got to work  towards achieving your goals every  single day forget about going on the 